WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.790
Speaker 1: We have updated vaccine polling
data from Monmouth University, we now know

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:10.679
that roughly one in five Americans still do
not want the covid vaccine.

00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:18.550
And those numbers are heavily and significantly
led by Republicans, 43 percent of whom still

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:22.000
do not want the covid vaccine and do not plan
to get it.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.660
If they can avoid it, I guess if they can
avoid it suggests something about if it became

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:31.200
a requirement for a job or to do something
they want to do, maybe they would get it.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.130
Overall, the good news is that the number
who don't want the vaccine is down, but it's

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.210
not really down dramatically.

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:41.070
Earlier in the pandemic, we saw significant
reductions in vaccine hesitancy is really

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.070
leveling out.

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:45.540
Now, the numbers are stunningly partizan.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:53.300
If you look at numbers by party, 43 percent
of Republicans do not want the vaccine, 22

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:58.260
percent of independents do not want the vaccine,
and just five percent of Democrats do not

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:00.440
want the vaccine.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.690
If it were all Democrats, we would get to
herd immunity.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:08.350
If it were all independents, we might it would
be 78 percent do.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:12.740
And if it were up to only Republicans, if
everybody believe what Republicans believe,

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:17.100
we would not get to herd immunity, although
maybe eventually we would, because so many

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.560
of them would get sick that they develop natural
immunity.

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.850
That's a different story, though.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.440
Many would die in that process.

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:26.670
Now, also interesting is that the racial gap
seems to almost have completely gone away,

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.549
at least according to this poll, 22 percent
of whites and 20 percent of people of color

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:33.260
don't want the vaccine.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:35.960
That is now essentially statistically equal.

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:40.869
There was a point in time at which there was
more of a gap led by vaccine hesitancy among

00:01:40.869 --> 00:01:42.960
the black American community.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.710
So the big takeaway is.

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:51.000
If 80 percent of the country plans to get
vaccinated, we can actually reach something

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.650
approximating approximating herd immunity,
which medical science believes.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:02:03.130
Again, it depends on how contagious is, whatever
variant becomes dominant and how sort of homogenous

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.560
versus heterogenous is vaccination.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:13.290
Somewhere between 70 and 85 percent vaccination
would be required to achieve herd.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:19.370
However, one thing we have to remember is
that vaccine opposition is not homogenous.

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:22.370
It varies greatly in different parts of the
country.

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:27.510
The Mississippi, Missouri, Massachusetts gap
right now is a really good example.

00:02:27.510 --> 00:02:31.090
92 percent of those in Massachusetts want
the vaccine.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:35.370
Mississippi is already at the point where
tons of vaccination appointments are going

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:36.560
unfilled.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:37.680
Demand is lagging.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:43.180
So you could end up with a situation where
some states are sort of extra vaccinated well

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:48.480
beyond what's required for herd immunity and
other states never reach it.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.780
And you have constant small clusters and outbreaks
which will just extend the pandemic.

00:02:53.780 --> 00:02:59.099
The sad part is that because some people don't
develop immunity, even when you get vaccinated,

00:02:59.099 --> 00:03:04.690
remember the 95 percent effective vaccine,
some others can't get the vaccine because

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:06.840
of specific medical conditions.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:12.709
You will have a situation where those who
could get it but just choose not to will give

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:18.720
the virus to some of the folks who either
got the vaccine but didn't develop immunity,

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:22.640
couldn't get the vaccine because of medical
condition, and some of them will die.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.840
That's that's the decision of anybody who
could get it and chooses not to.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:30.900
Is that you are increasing the odds that somebody
dies as a result of your actions.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:33.450
I'm glad I'm not participating in that.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.849
Other information from the poll approval for
Joe Biden so far is really looking pretty

00:03:37.849 --> 00:03:40.470
good, 54 percent approval for Biden.

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:46.730
Remember that Donald Trump never got to 50
percent approval even once during his presidency.

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:50.690
Sixty two percent approval for Joe Biden's
handling of the virus.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.800
That's up from 57 percent in March.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:57.630
There was the idea that it was up in March,
but it's going to go down as Biden becomes

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:58.640
the new normal.

00:03:58.640 --> 00:04:03.489
No covid approval for Biden continuing to
go up for comparison.

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:10.720
Biden at 62, Trump was at 34 percent approval
on covid when he left office and 63 percent

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.360
approval for Biden's covid stimulus bill,
which was passed last month.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.590
So the numbers are looking very solid for
Joe Biden.

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:23.199
I think getting infrastructure done would
boost them a little bit, but infrastructure

00:04:23.199 --> 00:04:25.660
is less visible to the average person.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.490
And it's also it takes longer than just something
gets passed and then you get fourteen hundred

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:30.490
bucks.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:33.029
So the impact on approval may be maybe lower.

00:04:33.029 --> 00:04:37.659
One last thought, the pause going on right
now on the Johnson and Johnson vaccine, which

00:04:37.659 --> 00:04:43.620
we talked about earlier this week, it is giving
a boost to the anti VAX people and it will

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:46.910
be something that we will have to wait and
see the effect of.

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:52.330
We see it impacting people anecdotally saying,
well, now I'm definitely never getting any

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:58.979
vaccine seeing that on social media, that
wasn't yet part of this polling information.

00:04:58.979 --> 00:05:06.270
So if we now see a reversal and vaccine hesitancy
goes up, it would be important to look at

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:10.849
whether the pause on the JMJ vaccine is a
factor in that

